## 9. Anticipated Challenges and Mitigation Strategies

| Challenge | Mitigation |
|-----------|------------|
| Estimating \( P_{\text{RFI}} \) from finite archival data | Use nonparametric density estimation (kernel methods) with convergence rates \( O(n^{-2/(d+4)}) \). Model selection via cross‑validation. |
| Defining the prior \( P(\mathcal{E}) \) without positive examples | Hierarchical priors with sensitivity analysis: report results over a range of plausible hyperparameters (e.g., optimistic, moderate, pessimistic Drake values). |
| Proving lower bounds for arbitrary drift rates | First prove for a restricted class (e.g., linear drift, known bandwidth) using communication complexity, then extend via reductions that preserve the bound. |
| Computational tractability of the Bayesian posterior | Use variational inference with a factorized approximation; bound the KL divergence from the true posterior via the evidence lower bound (ELBO). |
| Obtaining the unlabeled real sample \( U \) for domain adaptation | Collaborate with Breakthrough Listen and SKA teams to obtain a few hundred megabytes of “quiet” sky observations (already publicly available in part). |

